<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Masuria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Masuria is a lake district in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, part of the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-prussia">East Prussia</a>. Its many glacial lakes include Śniardwy and Mamry. Once the land of the Old Prussian Galindians, it was conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> and resettled from the 14th century, largely by Polish-speaking settlers from Mazovia, and it passed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> to Poland in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masuria.jpg" alt="Masuria" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: image/photo was taken by Wikipedia and Wikimedia Commons user Ludwig Schneider. I would appreciate being notified if ... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jezioro_Niegocin_w_okolicach_Gi%C5%BCycka_065.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
